From 7adb0a27e96ba91ce7d44f22600049946b0161a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:59:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 161/162] webrender: ES 2.0 on the PowerVR SGX530 itself

What the N950's driver (PowerVR SGX530, DDK 1.17) needs beyond Mesa's
ES 2.0 context:
- only the texture units the GPU has (8) are reset,
- no glMapBufferRange: repeated instances are built in a reused buffer
  and handed to glBufferData,
- no unsigned literals in GLSL ES 1.00, not even in a skipped #else,
- integer varyings: assigning to a component of the rounded conversion
  is no l-value. The vertex shader now works on a plain integer variable
  that a main wrapper (around the shader's renamed main) copies into the
  float varying, only where the varying is declared.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
